Cyberware.

Cyberware is machinery grafted into your own body. An installed implant
grants its bonuses, such as stats, resistances, or chance-based proc
effects, for as long as it stays inside you.

Every implant occupies one or more body locations: eyes, ears, brain,
skull, jaw, throat, neck, spine, heart, lungs, torso, skin, shoulders,
arms, hands, legs, and feet. Only one implant may occupy a location.

Implants also strain the body. No implant can cost more than 10 strain,
and the 24 cyberware locations create an absolute capacity of 240. Your
natural limit starts at 6 and grows with your level: one point per 10
levels, plus larger bonuses at levels 50, 100, 150, 200, and 250.
Cyber-touched origins grant 2 extra strain each, to a maximum of 10.
Each remort closes part of the distance between your natural limit and
240, reaching full capacity at remort 50. You cannot install an implant
that would push your total strain past your limit, and an implant may
demand a minimum level or stranger things before your body accepts it.

World cyberware comes in standard, refined, military, and artifact
qualities. Higher qualities provide more specialized or powerful benefits,
but source level still matters. Artifact systems may consume the maximum
strain or occupy several locations.

Commands:

cyberware [player]
  Show your installed implants, occupied body locations, and strain.
  Wizards may name a currently connected player to inspect that player's
  installed cyberware and strain.

cyberscan <implant>
  Inspect an implant's type, grade, body locations, strain, visibility,
  and proc count before installing it.

install <implant>
  Have a ripperdoc install an implant you are carrying.

extract <implant or location>
uninstall <implant or location>
  Have a ripperdoc remove an installed implant, returning it to your
  inventory.

Installation and extraction require a staffed ripperdoc clinic, and the
ripperdoc will not operate while you are fighting. The Forbidden Replacement
Table in Nethrys Undercity's Ripperdoc Quarter is a formal clinic. Cyberware
status and implant scans remain available anywhere. Use "engage ripperdoc"
at the clinic to review hardware, see the exact service fee, and confirm the
procedure.

Installation costs 10,000 coins per point of implant strain, with a 10,000
coin minimum. Extraction costs 5,000 coins per strain, with a 5,000 coin
minimum.

Installed implants cannot be dropped and stay with you across sessions. They
are hidden from normal inventory while installed, but remain visible through
cyberware or implants. Grade does not change persistence: standard, refined,
military, and artifact chrome all persist normally.

Only hardware explicitly created as temporary or nonpersistent is excluded,
and normal clinic installation rejects hardware that cannot be preserved. A
saved implant can be temporarily unavailable when its blueprint cannot load or
a one-of-a-kind implant is active elsewhere; its record remains for a later
retry. Only active restored implants consume strain, so missing or inactive
hardware releases its strain automatically.

Some implants are outwardly visible and anyone who looks at you will see them;
hidden ones stay your secret. Procs trigger on their own in combat: on your
hits, when you take damage, when you are badly hurt, or when you make a kill,
each with its own chance and cooldown.

General Tekal forbids cybernetics, so recoverable implants are uncommon and
normally expose an illicit source: contraband wetware, augmented criminals,
Green Door or Reca operatives, forbidden experiments, or repurposed machinery.
Specialists, elites, and named enemies are the usual sources of rarer hardware.
Shimmerdeep's Miura do not implant themselves; cyberware found there comes
from corrupted external machinery and mechaplants.

